{"timestamp": "2026-10-29T14:12:41.863113+00:00", "source": "hook", "event": "afterAgentResponse", "keys": ["cache_read_tokens", "cache_write_tokens", "conversation_id", "cursor_version", "generation_id", "hook_event_name", "input_tokens", "model", "model_id", "model_params", "output_tokens", "session_id", "text", "transcript_path", "user_email", "workspace_roots"], "fields": {"text": "Record 8 to 10 minutes with the app and the tests running. Restart the app before you start so `INV-1006` and `INV-1007` are still pending. The password for every demo account is `[redacted]`.\n\n**0:00 â€” Start the app**\n\nFrom the project folder:\n\n```powershell\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m uvicorn invoice_app.api.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5000\n```\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:5000.\n\nSay: \"A manager can sole-approve up to 50,000. A director can sole-approve up to 500,000. Above that, two different directors are required. A refused approval must leave the invoice unchanged.\"\n\n**1:00 â€” Manager refused at 75,000**\n\nSign in as `demo.manager`. Open the Approvals tab. Approve **Cedar Ridge Schools, INV-1006**, $75,000.00.\n\nThe alert should say a manager may approve up to 50,000.00 and the invoice was left unchanged. Open Invoices and show the row still **Pending Approval**.\n\n**2:30 â€” Director sole-approves that invoice**\n\nSign out. Sign in as `demo.director`. Approve INV-1006 again. It leaves the pending list and shows **Approved**.\n\n**3:30 â€” Two directors above 500,000**\n\nStay as `demo.director`. Approve **Northwind District, INV-1007**, $750,000.00.\n\nIt stays on the pending list, with one recorded vote: `demo.director (Director)`. The status is **Pending second approval**. `decidedBy` is still empty. Say that this first vote is a successful write, not a refusal.\n\nApprove INV-1007 again as the same director. The alert says the same user may never count as both approvers. The recorded vote is still only `demo.director`.\n\nSign out. Sign in as `demo.director2`. Approve INV-1007. It becomes **Approved**, with both directors listed.\n\n**6:30 â€” Unit tests, live**\n\nIn a second terminal, from the project folder:\n\n```powershell\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pytest\n```\n\nLeave the result on screen. Say that the suite covers the 50,000 and 500,000 boundaries, the same user voting twice, a non-director second vote, and a snapshot that proves a refusal writes nothing.\n\n**8:00 â"}}
